    # v383 (02/10/2026, evening) -- the operator's DECISION «prefiro a primeira opção»: the nine echo pairs OUTSIDE the ledger (examined routes); base v381. Inherited from v382: the operator's key: «O último elo incide no hamiltoniano oculto. O custo está no reflexo, o pagamento está na face no rosto, no nome» (the last link incides on the hidden Hamiltonian; the cost is in the reflection, the payment in the face, in the Name); R1–R6 ratified; the correction: «a TGL não é semi ela é ótica» (the TGL is optics, not semi-optics); the order: «isso mesmo, prossiga»; the v382 audits accepted
    _r2 = core.get("the_ledger_of_charges_v383") or {}
    _v2 = lambda d_: str(d_.get("verdict", "n/a")).replace("_", r"\_")
    _nv2 = lambda d_, t_: "" if d_.get("all_verified") is True else (r"\textbf{In this run %s did NOT close: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " % t_)
    _f2 = lambda x_, n_=3: (("%%.%df" % n_) % float(x_)) if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _e2 = lambda x_: (("%.2e" % float(x_)).replace("e-0", "e-").replace("e+0", "e+").replace("e-", r"\times10^{-").replace("e+", r"\times10^{") + "}") if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _kf2 = _r2.get("kernel_flags") or {}; _rt2 = _r2.get("runtime") or {}; _ct2 = _r2.get("counts") or {}; _cr2 = _r2.get("counts_in_rule") or {}; _bh2 = _r2.get("by_how") or {}; _pr2 = _r2.get("preregistration") or {}; _ld2 = _r2.get("ledger") or []
    _sh2 = lambda k_: str(((_pr2.get("sha256_read") or {}).get(k_) or "n/a"))[:16]
    _c2 = lambda i_: next((c_ for c_ in _ld2 if c_.get("id") == i_), {})
    _n2 = lambda i_, k_: (_c2(i_).get("numbers_read") or {}).get(k_)
    _tt2 = lambda x_: str(x_).replace("_", r"\_")
    _lado2 = {"reflexo": "reflection", "face": "face"}
    _lista2 = "; ".join(r"%s (%s, \texttt{%s})" % (c_.get("id"), _lado2.get(c_.get("side"), "n/a"), _tt2(c_.get("outcome"))) for c_ in _ld2)
    _reason2 = "; ".join(str(r_) for r_ in (_n2("F2", "reasons") or [])).replace("<", "$<$").replace(">", "$>$")
    _er2 = _r2.get("echo_routes_outside_the_ledger") or {}; _ro2 = _er2.get("routes") or []
    _amp2 = {"√β": r"$\sqrt{\bTGL}$", "sin 2θ": r"$\sin 2\theta_M$", "β": r"$\bTGL$"}
    _lei2 = {"KMS": r"KMS, $2\pi/\kappa$", "DEC": r"December, $2GM_f/(\bTGL c^3)$", "MAY": r"May, $(2GM_f/c^3)\ln(1/\bTGL)$"}
    _st2 = {"EXCLUDED_BY_DATA": "excluded by the data", "INCONCLUSIVE": "inconclusive"}
    _nr2 = lambda r_: (r_.get("numbers_read") or {})
    _rn2 = lambda r_: ((r", $z_{\rm excl}=" + _f2(_nr2(r_).get("z_excl"), 2) + "$" + ((r", blind O4 subsample (not independent) $" + _f2(_nr2(r_).get("z_excl_o4_cego"), 2) + "$") if _nr2(r_).get("z_excl_o4_cego") is not None else "")) if _nr2(r_).get("z_excl") is not None else ((r", relative systematic " + _f2(_nr2(r_).get("sist_rel"), 2)) if _nr2(r_).get("sist_rel") is not None else ""))
    _qual2 = lambda r_: (((r", the exclusion comes from amendment V4, which is not blind (controls with maximum $|z|$ of " + _f2((r_.get("numbers_read") or {}).get("controles_max_z"), 2) + r", below 5), and the V3 verdict pre-registered for the same pair is inconclusive") if (r_.get("id") == "ECO_e" and r_.get("qualifiers_ok")) else "")
                          + ((r", and by clause V5, which is in the pre-registration and was not applied by the pipeline, the reading would be underpowered and not falsified (power " + _f2((r_.get("qualifiers_read") or {}).get("power_R3"), 2) + r"$\sigma$)") if (r_.get("id") == "ECO_g" and r_.get("qualifiers_ok")) else ""))
    _rotas2 = "; ".join(r"%s: %s with %s, %s%s%s" % (_tt2(r_.get("id")), _amp2.get(str((r_.get("amplitude_from_preregistration") or {}).get("leitura")), "n/a"), _lei2.get(str((r_.get("delay_law_from_preregistration") or {}).get("nome")), "n/a"), _st2.get(r_.get("state"), "n/a"), _rn2(r_), _qual2(r_)) for r_ in _ro2)
    s.append(r"\paragraph*{Beside (v383) --- The ledger of charges and the viscosity: the TGL is optics, it reads the face and the cost; no outcome moves the rule; the pre-registration of both sides; the echo as a delayed copy outside the ledger.} " + _nv2(_r2, "the ledger of charges") +
             r"The operator gave the key (02/10/2026, verbatim in the program, in Portuguese; rendered here in English): the last link incides on the hidden Hamiltonian; the cost is in the reflection, the payment is in the face, in the Name. He ratified the six readings of the management (the $H_0$ register: $\bTGL$ once, in the reflection, bare background, node at $z_*$; the subject of the clocks is $K_\partial$, the hidden Hamiltonian; the neutrino's expert is the direct determination; the gate's final step is named by the payment; the estimand is $\delta\langle K_\partial\rangle$, read in the reflection, and on both sides by the optics correction that follows; branch B of the ringdown is closed) and corrected the management's view of sides: the TGL is not semi, it is optics; it reads the face as well as the cost; it allows reading both sides. Then the operator decided (02/10/2026, evening, verbatim in the program, in Portuguese: ``prefiro a primeira opção'', I prefer the first option): the nine pairs of the echo as a delayed copy are not charges of the theory and leave the ledger, as examined routes, with the numbers and the reason for each; v382, which carried them in the ledger beside, was sealed only in the canonical folder and is not custodied; this version starts from v381. "
             r"Two stones enter. \textsf{TGLExt.TheLedgerOfCharges} types the charge (side, reading law, reading, outcome in five words imposed by the type: \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED}, \texttt{FALSIFIED}, \texttt{INCONCLUSIVE}, \texttt{AWAITING}, \texttt{EXCLUDED\_IN\_READING}), the ledger (``one charge per reading law'' is a discipline of the concrete ledger, not of the type), and three facts stated as trivial by construction: the rule $\bTGL$ does not read the ledger (\textsf{the\_rule\_is\_constant\_in\_the\_ledger}, by \texttt{rfl}), with an extinguished charge the rule stays $\alpha\sqrt e$ (\textsf{falsified\_extinguishes\_the\_charge\_not\_the\_rule}; the hypothesis does not enter the proof, and that is what ``the rule does not read the ledger'' means), and the term $P=P$ (\textsf{the\_gate\_ignores\_the\_ledger}; that the gate's flags are a function of the formal alone is checked by the runtime's negative probes, not by this term); and the optics: $|\mathcal T|^2=\cos^2\theta$ is the face (the payment), $|\mathcal R|^2=\sin^2\theta$ is the reflection (the cost), $|\mathcal T|^2+|\mathcal R|^2=1$ (the S-$\partial$ theorem) and each side is the complement of the other (\textsf{the\_tgl\_is\_optics\_not\_semi}: the name is \textsf{[ONTO]}, the content is the identity written three times). That no side is blind and that what differs is the law of each reading and the instrument with power is the operator's correction \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}, not a theorem. The name of the final step by the payment is proposed beside (\textsf{finalStepNameProposed}); the gate does not change in this stone, renaming is the operator's act. "
             r"\textsf{TGLExt.ThePsionAndTheViscosity}: $\psi=\Omega$ is the psion, $\|\psi\|=1$ (a field of the certificate), $\langle\psi,\psi\rangle=1$ (proved by the reader's term, \textsf{reader\_reads\_the\_identity\_one}: the reader reads the identity as 1), $H_{\min}^{\rm mic}\psi=0$ (trivial by construction, $\Omega\in\mathbb C\Omega$; $H_{\min}^{\rm mic}$ is the minimal lock read on the hidden Hamiltonian $K=-\log\Delta$ of the light, which is \textsf{[KNOWN]} --- the kernel has $\Delta^{it}$ and its fixed set, not a definition of $K$; the zeros coincide, the operators do not; the content is the modular fixed line, v372) and the light fixes it; the continuous charge: transmitted $e^{-t\beta g}$ (the face in the flow), charged $1-e^{-t\beta g}$ (the reflection in the flow), summing to 1 at every $t$ (trivial by definition); the viscosity is the constant friction, $\tfrac{d}{dt}e^{-t\beta g}=-(\beta g)\,e^{-t\beta g}$, the coefficient $\beta g$ (a name \textsf{[ONTO]} on a computation); the charge never completes; no full static witness (an alias); and with $\beta$ of the rule the coefficient is $\alpha\sqrt e\,g$. The identification of $\beta g$ per modular time with $\Gamma_\omega=\tfrac12\bTGL\tau_\star\omega^2$ has no term: it is a reading \textsf{[ONTO]}; and that the gradient spectrum is read on $H_{\min}^{\rm mic}$ is the operator's key, with no term. "
             r"At runtime, the concrete ledger: " + str(len(_ld2)) + r" charges, one per reading law, each outcome read from the core in a stated way (" + str(_bh2.get("TOKEN_CONTAINS", "n/a")) + r" by the verdict's token, of the module or nested; " + str(_bh2.get("NUMBER_READ", "n/a")) + r" by a number read from the core with the rule stated; " + str(_bh2.get("DECLARED", "n/a")) + r" declared without a number) and equal to the one in the pre-registration of both sides V1.4, read by bytes (JSON \texttt{" + _sh2("json") + r"}, MD \texttt{" + _sh2("md") + r"}; published on the Bench; it supersedes V1.3 by the operator's decision, and the earlier ones by the audits' findings, before any new estimator or data): " + _lista2 + r". Counts: " + ", ".join(r"\texttt{%s} %s" % (_tt2(k_), v_) for k_, v_ in _ct2.items()) + r"; in the rule " + str(_r2.get("n_in_rule", "n/a")) + r" (" + ", ".join(r"\texttt{%s} %s" % (_tt2(k_), v_) for k_, v_ in _cr2.items() if v_) + (r"; no \texttt{FALSIFIED} in the ledger" if not _ct2.get("FALSIFIED") else "") + r"), beside " + str(_r2.get("n_beside", "n/a")) + r" (the cost placed on the face by convention). Outside the ledger, the " + str(_er2.get("n", "n/a")) + r" examined routes of the echo as a delayed copy, which are not charges of the theory (the state of each is read from the Phase 6 label in the core, the same one the v380 paragraph cites, and that label names the pair, not the theory; checked against V1.4): " + _rotas2 + r". The reason, read from the sources: the echo's amplitude equal to $|\mathcal R|$ is a reading \textsf{[ONTO]}, and the amplitude $\sin 2\theta_M$ is \textsf{[CONJECTURE]}; the KMS law takes the width $2\pi/\kappa$ of a strip in imaginary time as a real delay (audit of 28/09, GWECO-05); the December law is \textsf{[DECLARADO]}, derived by an AI, not from the axiom; the May law is \textsf{[INPUT]}, of May 2026; the three delay laws name the remnant's mass, and by the ratified reading R6 $\tau_\star=GM/c^3$ puts the cost on the face and contradicts the key (the link of that reading to the echo is \textsf{[DERIVED]}, a reading of the management); v381 already put the echo as a delayed copy outside the chain, and the operator's definition of 16/09, the echo as the boundary's response, stays. In the table of stones, the two stones appear as of v382: they were written and audited in v382, which stayed only in the canonical folder; they are public from this version on. R4 reads a frozen set without \texttt{FALSIFIED} (V11), the same source as the gate's experimental step. "
             r"The clocks' reading P2 is excluded by orders of magnitude without $n\sigma$ (\texttt{EXCLUDED\_IN\_READING}); R6 is inconclusive by the convergence control (parameters with $N<50\tau$: " + str(_c2("R6").get("control_read", "n/a")) + r", the control requires 0; a tension of " + _f2(_c2("R6").get("number_read"), 2) + r"$\sigma$ at the threshold; $\Delta\chi^2=+" + _f2(_n2("R6", "delta_chi2"), 2) + r"$ against $\Lambda$CDM; the $H_0$ sector of this convention is declared incompatible with that of R1, open); F2 is inconclusive by the measurement's systematic, not by power (the reason read from the core, in Portuguese: ``" + _reason2 + r"''; $\delta\tau=" + _f2(_n2("F2", "delta_tau"), 3) + r"\pm" + _f2(_n2("F2", "sigma"), 3) + r"$ against GR; in the canonical branch $\delta_A=" + _e2(_n2("F2", "delta_pred_A")) + r"$; the $0.2\sigma$ is the power of branch B, closed; that the cost is in the ringdown is a reading \textsf{[ONTO]} --- the core reads the canonical ringdown as the correspondence with GR, not as a test of $\bTGL$); F1 has a one-sided rule (the signed gain of the D1b law on the clocks: it falsifies only if $z\ge+5$; prior power " + _f2(_n2("F1", "poder_previo"), 2) + r"$\sigma$: powered by the Phase 4 yardstick, underpowered by the Phase 6 one); F4 follows the frozen kill rule (two independent determinations; the expert is JUNO); R2 awaits an estimator and has no power: $\Gamma(100\,\mathrm{Hz})=\tfrac12\bTGL t_{\rm P}\omega^2=" + _e2(_rt2.get("R2_gamma_100hz_per_s")) + r"\ \mathrm{s^{-1}}$, accumulated over 1 Gpc $" + _e2(_rt2.get("R2_gamma_accumulated_1gpc")) + r"$. "
             r"Sanity identities (not tests): $\cos^2\theta_M=" + _f2(_rt2.get("face_weight_cos2"), 6) + r"=1-\bTGL$, $\sin^2\theta_M=" + _f2(_rt2.get("reflection_weight_sin2"), 6) + r"=\bTGL$; $e^{-\bTGL}=" + _f2(_rt2.get("transmitted_t1_g1"), 6) + r"$ and its complement sum to 1; the two homonymous laws are distinct (in the angle, $\cos^2\theta_M$; in the flow, $e^{-\bTGL}$; they differ by $" + _e2(_rt2.get("angle_vs_flow_difference")) + r"\approx\bTGL^2/2$). Status: the key, the ratification and the correction are the operator's \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}; the stones are \textsf{[KERNEL]}, with the trivial stated as trivial; the ledger is read data \textsf{[REAL]}; nothing here confirms the TGL by nature. Proved $\neq$ confirmed; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} $\neq$ \texttt{CONFIRMED}. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v2(_r2) + r"}.")
